Drop rustfmt's rustc_driver dependency when targeting wasm.

rustfmt links rustc_driver for one reason, which its own comment states:
"Necessary to pull in object code as the rest of the rustc crates are shipped
only as rmeta files." That is a fact about how rustup distributes the rustc-dev
component, not about rustfmt. build.sh compiles the compiler crates from source
and gets real rlibs with object code in them, so the dependency has nothing left
to do - and rustc_driver itself is the one crate in the set that will not build
for wasm, since it reaches for a codegen backend.

Its only other use is install_ice_hook, which installs a panic handler that
prints a native backtrace and a bug-report URL. Neither is meaningful in a
module embedded in someone else's Node process.

Both hunks are conditional, so a host build of rustfmt is byte-for-byte the
build it was before this patch.

diff --git a/src/tools/rustfmt/src/bin/main.rs b/src/tools/rustfmt/src/bin/main.rs
index 6c48301f..06472653 100644
--- a/src/tools/rustfmt/src/bin/main.rs
+++ b/src/tools/rustfmt/src/bin/main.rs
@@ -25,9 +25,11 @@
 const BUG_REPORT_URL: &str = "https://github.com/rust-lang/rustfmt/issues/new?labels=bug";
 
 // N.B. these crates are loaded from the sysroot, so they need extern crate.
+#[cfg(not(target_family = "wasm"))]
 extern crate rustc_driver;
 
 fn main() {
+    #[cfg(not(target_family = "wasm"))]
     rustc_driver::install_ice_hook(BUG_REPORT_URL, |_| ());
 
     tracing_subscriber::fmt()
diff --git a/src/tools/rustfmt/src/lib.rs b/src/tools/rustfmt/src/lib.rs
index 942b42ec..a8e27e0d 100644
--- a/src/tools/rustfmt/src/lib.rs
+++ b/src/tools/rustfmt/src/lib.rs
@@ -19,6 +19,7 @@
 // Necessary to pull in object code as the rest of the rustc crates are shipped only as rmeta
 // files.
 #[allow(unused_extern_crates)]
+#[cfg(not(target_family = "wasm"))]
 extern crate rustc_driver;
 
 use std::cell::RefCell;
